message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite this repository and the thesis listed under references."
title: "Separating Partition, Leakage and Data Effects in Network Intrusion Detection Benchmarks: Code and Frozen Results"
abstract: "Code, frozen results and verification files for a study of how much of the difficulty of the official train/test splits of UNSW-NB15 and NSL-KDD comes from the split itself rather than from the attacks. The same records are split in four ways (official split, repeated cross-validation, and two size-matched random splits), with ten untuned classifiers, 1,100 fits and a seed noise floor for ranking changes."
